      "message": "Nit / follow-up (not blocking this change)\n\nThis patch correctly fixes the missing StatusIcon registration in the two firmware cards. While reviewing, I noticed the underlying reason FirmwareCardsBmc.vue was rendering the icon before this patch is a hidden coupling in BVToastMixin.js:\n\nBecause Vue merges a mixin\u0027s components into the consuming component, any file that mixes in BVToastMixin gets \u003cstatus-icon\u003e \"for free\" — even if the file never imports it itself. That is exactly why FirmwareCardsBmc.vue worked and FirmwareCardsBios.vue (which does not use the mixin) did not.\n\nWhy this matters (later, not now):\nIf someone ever removes StatusIcon from BVToastMixin, or migrates it to useToast in Composables, other views that use \u003cstatus-icon\u003e without a local import will silently break the same way FirmwareCardsBios.vue did.\n\nSuggested follow-up (separate change):\nGrep for \u003cstatus-icon across src/views/** and confirm each file has its own import StatusIcon from \u0027@/components/Global/StatusIcon\u0027. No action needed on this patch — scope is correct as-is.",
